/datum/job/roguetown/guildsman
	tutorial = "You are a member of the Pharovian Guild of Crafts, a massive guild formed to represent the interests of all craftsmen in the township of Pharos.\
	As a Guildsman, you hail from the three most important constituent guilds: The Smith's Guild, the Artificer's Guild, and the Architect's Guild. The Guildsmaster has sway over you, but it is not absolute."

/datum/job/roguetown/innkeeper
	tutorial = "Adventurers and warriors alike have two exit plans; the early grave or even earlier retirement. As the proud owner of this fine establishment, you took the latter: The Old Marks' Tavern and bathhouse! You even have an assortment of staff to help you, and plenty of business from the famished townsfolk looking to eat, weary travelers looking to rest, and characters of dubious repute seeking their own sort of success. Your bladework has gotten a little rusty, and the more devout tend to give you the odd evil eye for the extra 'delights' of the bathhouse--but, well...you can't win 'em all! Your time as an Innkeep have given you plenty of accesses to lucrative rumors. Access the Grand Contract Ledger to see what rumors to pass on to mammons hungry adventurers and mercenaries."

/datum/advclass/innkeeper
	tutorial = "Adventurers and warriors alike have two exit plans; the early grave or even earlier retirement. As the proud owner of this fine establishment, you took the latter: The Old Marks' tavern and bathhouse! You even have an assortment of staff to help you, and plenty of business from the famished townsfolk looking to eat, weary travelers looking to rest, and characters of dubious repute seeking their own sort of success. Your bladework has gotten a little rusty, and the more devout tend to give you the odd evil eye for the extra 'delights' of the bathhouse--but, well...you can't win 'em all!"

/datum/job/roguetown/wapprentice
	tutorial = "Yils of study have led you to the University-Under-the-Scar. The Divine heals and protects. \
	The arcyne arts, though useful, are far more suited to death and destruction. The Crown knows this, \
	and provides a stipend to fund your studies and just as much your complacency, to not turn your \
	magicks against the Crown. A comfortable tenure, a stipend, and a place to undergo your study. \
	What more could a Mage ask for?"

/datum/advclass/wapprentice/associate/apprentice
	tutorial = "The road to arcyne mastery is long and treacherous. Books, scrolls, gems, studies, \
	singed hair, and summoning gone wrong. Expenses and death abound; it is not a path for the pauper \
	or the coward. You, however, were given a place as an apprentice in the University-Under-the-Scar. \
	Under the watchful gaze of the Court Magician and their associates, you may yet live \
	to become a master of the arcyne arts. And even in the most rote of chores, there is knowledge to be found..."

/datum/job/roguetown/merchant
	tutorial = "Some find craft fulfilling, others take to powerful magic, and yet others take to war and steel. But you found a different vocation. You understand numbers, you understand trade, and you know how to close a good deal. Through expertise - or perhaps a well-placed connection - you have risen to the second most powerful position in the century-old Pharovian Trading Company, second only to the Grand Factor, who keeps the Company's seat at Rosporth, a leased enclave a few days' ride north of the Scar.\n\
You are the beating heart of the economy of Pharos, inheritor of a thousand yils of her people's sailing traditions. Without you, Malumite craftsmen's wares would have nowhere to go, the grain blessed by Astrata and Dendor would rot in the fields, and the perfumes and spices promised to us by Eora would never reach our shores.\n\
The priests will whisper that you follow the Sun-Thief. Frown, shake your head, and remind them you are an honest and humble merchant keeping the wheels of commerce turning, a faithful worker of Malum's will. Do not let some mouth-breathing crownsman tell you otherwise."

